            "review_title": "Review at KAMPONG - Hainanese Chicken Rice",
            "review_text": "Khoai Lang Mật\nPhan Thiet, Vietnam9 contributions\n0\nTrying something different for lunch\nSep 2026 • Family\nSix of us from the office went to Kampong for lunch today to have a change from our usual meals. We normally order Hainanese chicken rice, so this time we decided to try some other dishes, including the baked chicken with cheese and the salmon salad with passion fruit dressing. The salad was light, and the slightly sour passion fruit dressing helped keep it from feeling too rich. The baked chicken was quite cheesy, and that ended up being the favorite among some of the girls in our group. The restaurant was busy during lunch, but the staff kept things moving. The dishes didn't all arrive at exactly the same time, but we didn't have to wait too long. Overall, it was a convenient place for a casual lunch with colleagues.\nRead more\nWritten September 10, 2026",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
